# A change to one of these files needs the owner's review, since main's
# ruleset requires review from code owners. Every other file, the other
# workflows included, merges on its checks and the work rules alone.
# This file guards itself.
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @AlokBansal8

# The release rules (README.md, "Releasing").
/.github/workflows/release.yml      @AlokBansal8
/.github/workflows/version-rule.yml @AlokBansal8
/scripts/version-rule.mjs           @AlokBansal8
/README.md                          @AlokBansal8

# What the mutation gate judges: its lanes, their Stryker configs, and the
# script that plans the lanes with work. A pull request runs its own copy, so
# it could drop or narrow the lane that would judge it. The gate's workflow,
# .github/workflows/mutation.yml, is not here: niyam's shared Guard judges it
# against the approved slice, as it does every .github/ change. Not covered:
# the @veda-hq/agnipariksha pin in package.json, whose planner the script
# calls. Pins stay agents' work, and released-pins.mjs holds each to an exact
# release.
/agnipariksha.json                  @AlokBansal8
/stryker/                           @AlokBansal8
/packages/*/stryker.config.mjs      @AlokBansal8
/scripts/mutation-lanes.mjs         @AlokBansal8

# The kavach Python mutation gate's list of mutants no test can kill, each
# with the outcome it gets (veda#558). A row lets a mutant on a changed line
# pass, so adding one waits for the owner's review. The gate's workflow,
# .github/workflows/kavach-python-mutation.yml, and its script,
# scripts/kavach_mutation/, are not here: niyam's Guard judges the workflow
# against the approved slice, and the slice names only the list.
/packages/kavach/python/mutation-equivalents.tsv @AlokBansal8

# What veda's lint enforces and what it forgives: the rules, and the findings
# suppressed when they were turned on. Turning a rule off or adding a
# suppression waits for the owner's review too.
/eslint.config.js                   @AlokBansal8
/eslint-suppressions.json           @AlokBansal8
